* Backs: os9-dev/references/6809/syscalls-and-module-format.md and
*        os9-dev/references/common/ipc.md, "reserved vs. user-definable"
*        signal-code range dispute (some sources say 4-255, one says 128-255)
* Tests: whether the kernel enforces any boundary on signal delivery, or
*        whether "reserved" is a documentation-only convention. Installs
*        an intercept handler, sends itself code 50 (disputed range) and
*        code 200 (undisputed user-definable), and prints which code the
*        handler actually received.
*
* Result observed on NitrOS-9 (6809), via nitros9repl.sh + asm:
*   GOT 50
*   GOT 200
* Both F$Send calls succeeded (carry clear) and the handler correctly
* matched each code in turn (no SEND1/SEND2 FAILED, no GOT UNKNOWN) --
* the kernel delivers code 50 and code 200 identically. "Reserved" is a
* Microware documentation/naming convention only, not kernel-enforced.

 nam sigtest
 mod modend+3,nm,$11,$81,start,$0100
nm fcs /SIGTEST/
start equ *
 leax hndlr,pcr
 ldu #0
 swi2
 fcb $09          F$Icpt: install handler (X=routine, U=storage)
 swi2
 fcb $0C          F$ID: A=own PID
 ldb #50
 swi2
 fcb $08          F$Send: A=dest PID (self), B=signal code 50
 bcc ok1
 leax fail1,pcr
 ldy #40
 lda #1
 swi2
 fcb $8C
ok1 equ *
 swi2
 fcb $0C
 ldb #200
 swi2
 fcb $08          F$Send code 200 (undisputed user-definable range)
 bcc ok2
 leax fail2,pcr
 ldy #40
 lda #1
 swi2
 fcb $8C
ok2 equ *
 clrb
 swi2
 fcb $06          F$Exit
hndlr equ *
 cmpb #50
 beq hlo
 cmpb #200
 beq hhi
 leax hunk,pcr
 bra hprint
hlo leax hlomsg,pcr
 bra hprint
hhi leax hhimsg,pcr
hprint ldy #40
 lda #1
 swi2
 fcb $8C          I$WritLn: A=path, Y=length -- note it terminates on a
*                  literal $0D byte, NOT FCS's sign-bit convention (see
*                  the fcb $0D after each message below -- a real gotcha
*                  found while debugging this test's first garbled run)
 rti
hlomsg fcs /GOT 50/
 fcb $0D
hhimsg fcs /GOT 200/
 fcb $0D
hunk fcs /GOT UNKNOWN/
 fcb $0D
fail1 fcs /SEND1 FAILED/
 fcb $0D
fail2 fcs /SEND2 FAILED/
 fcb $0D
modend equ *
 emod
